    <!--
      PRODUCTION SEED - it ships demo accounts with published passwords.

      This is a portfolio deployment. Being browsable by someone who has never met me IS the
      purpose of this environment, so the seed belongs in the only context that environment
      runs. A system with real customers would seed nothing here and provision the first admin
      out of band.

      WHAT RUNS WHEN
        - 001 seeds the bike catalogue once. Reference data, it never changes.
        - 002/003/004 are runAlways: they re-assert the demo state on every application start.
          Liquibase normally runs a changeset once, which would freeze the dates at first boot -
          three months later the dashboard would read 0 active rentals and 0% occupancy, and a
          recruiter opening the link on their own schedule would see a dead site. These three
          re-anchor everything to CURRENT_DATE instead.

      CONSEQUENCE, STATED PLAINLY: changeset 004 deletes every reservation in the database on
      each boot, including any a visitor created. On a demo box that is the point - the tour
      resets to its scripted state and stays repeatable. It is also why none of this may ever be
      pointed at a database holding real bookings.

      See DEMO.md for the walkthrough these fixtures exist to support.
    -->

